Subject: Competitive play: a set's game passes its menus unseen
Upstream-base: a353c8f2dfb34eb08fecd725965a46ea629428e3

A set's game goes through the retail online flow by itself (0047), and the
player used to watch it click through the title, the main menu, the online
Mii list and the Mii's card. Those screens still run and do their work (the
online save, the Mii's save slot, the save), but FERender::RenderScene skips
them while the game passes them by itself, as No HUD (0021) skips the match's
overlays: the title and the main menu once a set is on its way, and from the
main menu's Online on also the Mii list, the Mii's card, the navigation bar
and the popups over the Mii screens. The player sees the frontend's own
camera move to the online area, the WFC login's Connecting screen and the
draft. The module also keeps the menu sounds of those screens silent
(src/platform/competitive_match.cpp). A set whose Mii is not on the computer
shows every screen: the player chooses the Mii.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_competitive.h b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
--- a/include/mscharged_competitive.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
@@ -64,6 +64,12 @@ int mscharged_competitive_popup(int type);
 // The front end is back from an online match (the series is over).
 void mscharged_competitive_back_from_game(void);
 #endif
+
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// A front-end scene about to be drawn (the FEScene hash of its file): true
+// while a set's game passes it by itself (tweak patch 0048): not drawn.
+bool mscharged_competitive_hides_scene(unsigned long scene);
+#endif
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
diff --git a/src/Game/FE/feRender.cpp b/src/Game/FE/feRender.cpp
--- a/src/Game/FE/feRender.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/FE/feRender.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,9 @@
 #include "NL/nlString.h"
 #include "NL/platvmath.h"
 #include "mscharged_tweaks.h"
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+#include "mscharged_competitive.h"
+#endif
 
 static nlFloatColour s_currentAssetColour;
 static const nlVector3 s_quadPositions[4] = {
@@ -242,6 +245,13 @@ void FERender::RenderScene(FEScene* scene)
         return;
     }
 #endif
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Competitive play: the screens a set's game passes by itself.
+    if (mscharged_competitive_hides_scene(scene->m_uHashID))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
 
     m_pRenderScene = scene;
     s_currentAssetColour.c[0] = 1.0f;
